18. String Operators This operator is used for the concatenation of 2 or more strings using the concatenation operator ('.'). We can also use the concatenating assignment operator ('.=') to append the argument on the right side to the argument on the left side.OperatorNameSyntaxOperation.Concatenation$x.$yConcatenated $x and $y.=Concatenation and assignment$x.=$yFirst, it concatenates then assigns, the same as $x = $x.$yExample: This example describes the string operator in PHP.
            PHP

    <?php
  $x = "Geeks";
  $y = "for";
  $z = "Geeks!!!";
  echo $x . $y . $z, "\n";
  $x .= $y . $z;
  echo $x;
?>

OutputGeeksforGeeks!!!
GeeksforGeeks!!!
